H5100.definition:
feminine of H5099 (נַהַם);
snarling
KJV: disquietness, roaring.

H5101.definition:
a primitive root;
to bray (as an ass), scream (from hunger)
KJV: bray.

H5102.definition:
a primitive root;
to sparkle, i.e. (figuratively) be cheerful; hence (from the sheen of a running stream) to flow, i.e. (figuratively) assemble
KJV: flow (together), be lightened.

H5103.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H5102 (נָהַר);
a river, especially the Euphrates
KJV: river, stream.

H5104.definition:
from H5102 (נָהַר);
a stream (including the sea; expectation the Nile, Euphrates, etc.); figuratively, prosperity
KJV: flood, river.

H5105.definition:
from H5102 (נָהַר) in its original sense;
daylight
KJV: light.

H5106.definition:
a primitive root;
to refuse, forbid, dissuade, or neutralize
KJV: break, disallow, discourage, make of none effect.

H5107.definition:
a primitive root;
to germinate, i.e. (figuratively) to (causatively, make) flourish; also (of words), to utter
KJV: bring forth (fruit), make cheerful, increase.

H5108.definition:
or נֵיב; from H5107 (נוּב);
produce, literally or figuratively
KJV: fruit.

H5109.definition:
from H5108 (נוֹב); fruitful;
Nobai, an Israelite
KJV: Nebai (from the margin).

H5110.definition:
a primitive root;
to nod, i.e. waver; figuratively, to wander, flee, disappear; also (from shaking the head in sympathy), to console, deplore, or (from tossing the head in scorn) taunt
KJV: bemoan, flee, get, mourn, make to move, take pity, remove, shake, skip for joy, be sorry, vagabond, way, wandering.

H5111.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5116 (נָוֶה);
to flee
KJV: get away.

H5112.definition:
(only defective נֹד ); from H5110 (נוּד);
exile
KJV: wandering.

H5113.definition:
the same as H5112 (נוֹד)lemma נוֹדּ extra dagesh, corrected to נוֹד; vagrancy;
Nod, the land of Cain
KJV: Nod.

H5114.definition:
from H5068 (נָדַב); noble;
Nodab, an Arab tribe
KJV: Nodab.

H5116.definition:
or (feminine) נָוָה; from H5115 (נָוָה);
(adjectively) at home; hence (by implication of satisfaction) lovely; also (noun) a home, of God (temple), men (residence), flocks (pasture), or wild animals (den)
KJV: comely, dwelling (place), fold, habitation, pleasant place, sheepcote, stable, tarried.

H5117.definition:
a primitive root;
to rest, i.e. settle down; used in a great variety of applications, literal and figurative, intransitive, transitive and causative (to dwell, stay, let fall, place, let alone, withdraw, give comfort, etc.)
KJV: cease, be confederate, lay, let down, (be) quiet, remain, (cause to, be at, give, have, make to) rest, set down. Compare H3241 (יָנִים).

H5118.definition:
or נוֹחַ; from H5117 (נוּחַ);
quiet
KJV: rest(-ed, -ing place).

H5119.definition:
feminine of H5118 (נוּחַ); quietude;
Nochah, an Israelite
KJV: Nohah.

H5121.definition:
from H5115 (נָוָה); residence;
Navith, a place in Palestine
KJV: Naioth (from the margin).

H5122.definition:
(Aramaic) or נְוָלִי; (Aramaic), from an unused root probably meaning to be foul;
a sink
KJV: dunghill.

H5123.definition:
a primitive root;
to slumber (from drowsiness)
KJV: sleep, slumber.

H5125.definition:
a primitive root;
to resprout, i.e. propagate by shoots; figuratively, to be perpetual
KJV: be continued.

H5127.definition:
a primitive root;
to flit, i.e. vanish away (subside, escape; causatively, chase, impel, deliver)
KJV: [idiom] abate, away, be displayed, (make to) flee (away, -ing), put to flight, [idiom] hide, lift up a standard.

H5128.definition:
a primitive root;
to waver, in a great variety of applications, literally and figuratively (as subjoined)
KJV: continually, fugitive, [idiom] make, to (go) up and down, be gone away, (be) move(-able, -d), be promoted, reel, remove, scatter, set, shake, sift, stagger, to and fro, be vagabond, wag, (make) wander (up and down).

H5129.definition:
from H3259 (יָעַד) and H3050 (יָהּ); convened of Jah;
Noadjah, the name of an Israelite, and a false prophetess
KJV: Noadiah.

H5130.definition:
a primitive root;
to quiver (i.e. vibrate up and down, or rock to and fro); used in a great variety of applications (including sprinkling, beckoning, rubbing, bastinadoing, sawing, waving, etc.)
KJV: lift up, move, offer, perfume, send, shake, sift, strike, wave.

H5131.definition:
from H5130 (נוּף);
elevation
KJV: situation. Compare H5297 (נֹף).

H5132.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to flash; hence, to blossom (from the brilliancy of color); also, to fly away (from the quickness of motion)
KJV: flee away, bud (forth).

H5133.definition:
or נֹצָה; feminine active participle of H5327 (נָצָה) in the sense of flying;
a pinion (or wing feather); often (collectively) plumage
KJV: feather(-s), ostrich.

H5134.definition:
a primitive root;
to suckle
KJV: nurse.

H5135.definition:
(Aramaic) from an unused root (corresponding to that of H5216 (נִיר)) meaning to shine;
fire
KJV: fiery, fire.

H5136.definition:
a primitive root;
to be sick, i.e. (figuratively) distressed
KJV: be full of heaviness.

H5137.definition:
a primitive root;
to spirt, i.e. besprinkle (especially in expiation)
KJV: sprinkle.

H5138.definition:
from H2102 (זוּד);
something boiled, i.e. soup
KJV: pottage.

H5139.definition:
or נָזִר; from H5144 (נָזַר);
separate, i.e. consecrated (as prince, a Nazirite); hence (figuratively from the latter) an unpruned vine (like an unshorn Nazirite)
KJV: Nazarite (by a false alliteration with Nazareth), separate(-d), vine undressed.

H5140.definition:
a primitive root;
to drip, or shed by trickling
KJV: distil, drop, flood, (cause to) flow(-ing), gush out, melt, pour (down), running water, stream.

H5141.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain meaning;
a nose-ring
KJV: earring, jewel.

H5142.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to the root of H5143 (נֵזֶק);
to suffer (causatively, inflict) loss
KJV: have (en-) damage, hurt(-ful).

H5143.definition:
from an unused root meaning to injure;
loss
KJV: damage.

H5144.definition:
a primitive root;
to hold aloof, i.e. (intransitivey) abstain (from food and drink, from impurity, and even from divine worship (i.e. apostatize)); specifically, to set apart (to sacred purposes), i.e. devote
KJV: consecrate, separate(-ing, self).

H5145.definition:
or נֵזֶר; from H5144 (נָזַר);
properly, something set apart, i.e. (abstractly) dedication (of a priet or Nazirite); hence (concretely) unshorn locks; also (by implication) a chaplet (especially of royalty)
KJV: consecration, crown, hair, separation.

H5146.definition:
the same as H5118 (נוּחַ); rest;
Noach, the patriarch of the flood
KJV: Noah.

H5147.definition:
from H2247 (חָבָה); occult;
Nachbi, an Israelite
KJV: Nakbi.

H5148.definition:
a primitive root;
to guide; by implication, to transport (into exile, or as colonists)
KJV: bestow, bring, govern, guide, lead (forth), put, straiten.

H5149.definition:
from H5162 (נָחַם); comforted;
Nechum, an Israelite
KJV: Nehum.

H5150.definition:
or נִחֻם; from H5162 (נָחַם);
properly, consoled; abstractly, solace
KJV: comfort(-able), repenting.

H5151.definition:
from H5162 (נָחַם); comfortable;
Nachum, an Israelite prophet
KJV: Nahum.

H5152.definition:
from the same as H5170 (נַחַר); snorer;
Nochor, the name of the grandfather and a brother of Abraham
KJV: Nahor.

H5153.definition:
apparently passive participle of H5172 (נָחַשׁ) (perhaps in the sense of ringing), i.e. bell-metal; or from the red color of the throat of a serpent (H5175 (נָחָשׁ), as denominative) when hissing);
coppery, i.e. (figuratively) hard
KJV: of brass.

H5154.definition:
or נְחֻשָׁה; feminine of H5153 (נָחוּשׁ);
copper
KJV: brass, steel. Compare H5176 (נָחָשׁ).

H5155.definition:
probably denominative from H2485 (חָלִיל);
a flute
KJV: (plural) Nehiloth.

H5156.definition:
from the same as H5170 (נַחַר);
a nostril
KJV: (dual) nostrils.

H5157.definition:
a primitive root;
to inherit (as a (figurative) mode of descent), or (generally) to occupy; causatively, to bequeath, or (generally) distribute, instate
KJV: divide, have (inheritance), take as a heritage, (cause to, give to, make to) inherit, (distribute for, divide (for, for an, by), give for, have, leave for, take (for)) inheritance, (have in, cause to, be made to) possess(-ion).

H5158.definition:
or (feminine) נַחְלָה; (Psalm 124:4), or נַחֲלָה; (Ezekiel 47:19; Ezekiel 48:28), from H5157 (נָחַל) in its original sense;
a stream, especially a winter torrent; (by implication) a (narrow) valley (in which a brook runs); also a shaft (of a mine)
KJV: brook, flood, river, stream, valley.

H5159.definition:
from H5157 (נָחַל) (in its usual sense);
properly, something inherited, i.e. (abstractly) occupancy, or (concretely) an heirloom; generally an estate, patrimony or portion
KJV: heritage, to inherit, inheritance, possession. Compare H5158 (נַחַל).

H5160.definition:
from H5158 (נַחַל) and H410 (אֵל); valley of God;
Nachaliel, a place in the Desert
KJV: Nahaliel.

H5161.definition:
apparently a patronymic from an unused name (apparently passive participle of H2492 (חָלַם)); dreamed;
a Nechelamite, or descendant of Nechlam
KJV: Nehelamite.

H5162.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to sigh, i.e. breathe strongly; by implication, to be sorry, i.e. (in a favorable sense) to pity, console or (reflexively) rue; or (unfavorably) to avenge (oneself)
KJV: comfort (self), ease (one's self), repent(-er,-ing, self).

H5163.definition:
from H5162 (נָחַם); consolation;
Nacham, an Israelite
KJV: Naham.

H5164.definition:
from H5162 (נָחַם);
ruefulness, i.e. desistance
KJV: repentance.

H5166.definition:
from H5162 (נָחַם) and H3050 (יָהּ); consolation of Jah;
Nechemjah, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Nehemiah.

H5167.definition:
from H5162 (נָחַם); consolatory;
Nachamani, an Israelite
KJV: Nahamani.

H5169.definition:
a primitive root;
to be urgent
KJV: require haste.

H5170.definition:
and (feminine) נַחֲרָה; from an unused root meaning to snort or snore;
a snorting
KJV: nostrils, snorting.

H5171.definition:
or נַחְרַי; from the same as H5170 (נַחַר); snorer;
Nacharai or Nachrai, an Israelite
KJV: Naharai, Nahari.

H5172.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to hiss, i.e. whisper a (magic) spell; generally, to prognosticate
KJV: [idiom] certainly, divine, enchanter, (use) [idiom] enchantment, learn by experience, [idiom] indeed, diligently observe.

H5173.definition:
from H5172 (נָחַשׁ);
an incantation or augury
KJV: enchantment.

H5174.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5154 (נְחוּשָׁה);
copper
KJV: brass.

H5175.definition:
from H5172 (נָחַשׁ);
a snake (from its hiss)
KJV: serpent.

H5176.definition:
the same as H5175 (נָחָשׁ);
Nachash, the name of two persons apparently non-Israelite
KJV: Nahash.

H5177.definition:
from H5172 (נָחַשׁ); enchanter;
Nachshon, an Israelite
KJV: Naashon, Nahshon.

H5178.definition:
for H5154 (נְחוּשָׁה);
copper, hence, something made of that metal, i.e. coin, a fetter; figuratively, base (as compared with gold or silver)
KJV: brasen, brass, chain, copper, fetter (of brass), filthiness, steel.

H5179.definition:
from H5178 (נְחֹשֶׁת); copper;
Nechushta, an Israelitess
KJV: Nehushta.

H5180.definition:
from H5178 (נְחֹשֶׁת);
something made of copper, i.e. the copper serpent of the Desert
KJV: Nehushtan.

H5181.definition:
a primitive root;
to sink, i.e. descend; causatively, to press or lead down
KJV: be broken, (cause to) come down, enter, go down, press sore, settle, stick fast.

H5182.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5181 (נָחַת);
to descend; causatively, to bring away, deposit, depose
KJV: carry, come down, depose, lay up, place.

H5183.definition:
from H5182 (נְחַת); also (intransitively; perhaps from H5117 (נוּחַ))
a descent, i.e. imposition, unfavorable (punishment) or favorable (food); restfulness
KJV: lighting down, quiet(-ness), to rest, be set on.

H5184.definition:
the same as H5183 (נַחַת); quiet;
Nachath, the name of an Edomite and of two Israelites
KJV: Nahath.

H5185.definition:
from H5181 (נָחַת);
descending
KJV: come down.

H5186.definition:
a primitive root;
to stretch or spread out; by implication, to bend away (including moral deflection); used in a great variety of application
KJV: [phrase] afternoon, apply, bow (down, -ing), carry aside, decline, deliver, extend, go down, be gone, incline, intend, lay, let down, offer, outstretched, overthrown, pervert, pitch, prolong, put away, shew, spread (out), stretch (forth, out), take (aside), turn (aside, away), wrest, cause to yield.

H5187.definition:
from H5190 (נָטַל);
laden
KJV: that bear.

H5188.definition:
from H5197 (נָטַף);
a pendant for the ears (especially of pearls)
KJV: chain, collar.

H5189.definition:
from H5203 (נָטַשׁ);
a tendril (as an offshoot)
KJV: battlement, branch, plant.

H5190.definition:
a primitive root;
to lift; by implication, to impose
KJV: bear, offer, take up.

H5191.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H5190 (נָטַל);
to raise
KJV: take up.

H5192.definition:
; from H5190 (נָטַל);
a burden
KJV: weighty.

H5193.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to strike in, i.e. fix; specifically, to plant (literally or figuratively)
KJV: fastened, plant(-er).

H5194.definition:
from H5193 (נָטַע);
a plant; collectively, a plantation; abstractly, a planting
KJV: plant.

H5195.definition:
from H5193 (נָטַע);
a plant
KJV: plant.

H5196.definition:
plural of H5194 (נֶטַע);
Netaim, a place in Palestine
KJV: plants.

H5197.definition:
a primitive root;
to ooze, i.e. distil gradually; by implication, to fall in drops; figuratively, to speak by inspiration
KJV: drop(-ping), prophesy(-et).

H5198.definition:
from H5197 (נָטַף);
a drop; specifically, an aromatic gum (probably stacte)
KJV: drop, stacte.

H5199.definition:
from H5197 (נָטַף); distillation;
Netophah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Netophah.
